i am 24 years old i am one of the five  people who are stuck in the flood  i can never forget the 25th of august it  was a horrific day for us it was early  morning and it was raining heavily so i  decided to move my vehicle to a safe  place when i came down my friends also  joined me we were moving towards the  bazaar with our vehicles  we saw the torrent heading towards us  so we ran and climbed a big rock to seek  refuge we were soon surrounded by raging  waters  we called the deputy commissioner office  to tell them that we were stuck on a  rock and for god's sake to help us  because our lives were at stake  for five hours but there was no response  my friends were all panicking and were  crying  bilal was scared and called his father  and told him baba  i have been a disobedient son please  forgive me i will not survive i am in a  struggle of life and death pray for me  were also crying and calling their  families to tell them that their lives  were in danger and to pray for them  anwar offered his prayers on a rock  while the others were reciting verses  from the quran  just across from our villagers and  family members were trying to throw  ropes to save us my friends told me i  should grab their open go first and they  tied me up  suddenly a big wave came smashing on the  rock and i was able to cling onto the  rope but all my friends were swept away  it is very painful for me that i could  not do anything for my friends  there was a helicopter for rescue my  friends would still be alive and with me  my friends were lost because of  negligence of the authorities  when i got out of the tour and my family  thanked allah and told me that our home  vehicles shops and fields were all gone  after the incident i felt in my heart  that i should stand up for my people to  the last breath and by allah's help to  serve my people  our pakistani brothers and sisters are  sending aid and i am helping with  distribution of food and medicine it is  my duty i have nothing left but i will  do whatever i can for my people i have  dedicated my life to my people
 

